10. Retry Strategy

Retry behavior should not be based only on whether an exception occurred.

Ask:

If exactly the same request is executed again later, is there a reasonable possibility that it will succeed?

10.1 Generally Retryable

HTTP 429
HTTP 502
HTTP 503
HTTP 504
Connection reset
Temporary network failure
Upstream timeout
Database deadlock
Temporary service unavailable

10.2 Generally Not Retryable

Invalid parameter
Missing business parameter
Account not found
Permission denied
Business rule violation
Invalid authentication
Programming error
Unexpected KeyError
Unexpected NoneType failure

10.3 Retryability Matrix

Missing parameter
Retry: No
Action: Correct parameter
Invalid account ID
Retry: No
Action: Correct parameter
Account not found
Retry: No
Action: Ask user / change parameter
Business rule violation
Retry: No
Action: Inform user
HTTP 429
Retry: Yes
Action: Retry with backoff
HTTP 502 / 503 / 504
Retry: Yes
Action: Retry with backoff
Upstream timeout
Retry: Yes
Action: Retry with backoff
DB deadlock
Retry: Usually
Action: Retry
Permission denied
Retry: No
Action: Correct authorization
Authentication failure
Retry: Usually no
Action: Re-authenticate
Unexpected programming error
Retry: No
Action: Internal investigation

